  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d4ecd1a615a340f4c9104ca01624d106, type: 3}
  m_Name: BlueRedButton
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::YourCall.Dilemma
  _id: blue_red_button
  _verb: 2
  _weight: 2
  _narratorPrompt: You spent a whole life deciding what other people deserved. It
    would be a waste to let all that practice rot now. So. A room of the newly dead,
    two buttons on the wall, one rule. If more than half of them pressed [blue]blue[/blue],
    the [blue]blue[/blue] souls live. If fewer than half, only the [red]red[/red]
    souls walk out. Every one of them has already chosen, except this one, and its
    button is left to you. Press [blue]blue[/blue] and you [amber]gamble[/amber]
    it on the room. Press [red]red[/red] and it lives for [amber]certain[/amber],
    whatever the room did. You are not choosing for yourself. There is nothing of
    yours left to lose. Your call.
  _choices:
  - _id: blue
    _label: blue
    _narratorReact: You pressed [blue]blue[/blue], and threw that soul in with the
      room, and the room held. More than half of them chose [blue]blue[/blue] for
      a stranger, so it walks out among them. You trusted a roomful of the dead with
      a life, and this once they did not let you down. Do not get used to the feeling.
    _narratorReactStruck: You pressed [blue]blue[/blue], and gambled that soul on
      the room, and the room came up short. Fewer than half had pressed [blue]blue[/blue],
      so the [blue]blue[/blue] souls stayed behind, and the one you chose for is
      gone. You bet a stranger on strangers, and they folded. A whole career weighing
      what people deserved, and this is what the practice bought.
    _struckParty: 
    _gambledParty: charge
    _route: 
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 3
      _value: 1
    - _axis: 0
      _value: 1
  - _id: red
    _label: red
    _narratorReact: You pressed [red]red[/red], and that soul is safe, whatever the
      room did. You would not put a single life in the hands of strangers. All those
      years judging what people deserved, and you still trust no hand but your own.
      It lives, and you will never know whether the room would have carried it. Sit
      with that.
    _narratorReactStruck: 
    _struckParty: 
    _gambledParty: 
    _route: 
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 3
      _value: -1
  _statsHeading: how the room voted
  _roomBlueFraction: 0.43
  _crowdThreshold: 0.5
  _thresholdLabel: half
